From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:55:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 251/274] Vocabulary-parallel drafting: mix the step into the
 seed, as the full-vocab draft does

The backport of vllm-project/vllm#61161 (ad6c55362) puts the draft step in the
seed's high word in the full-vocab draft sampler, DFlash2 and the rejection
sampler, so block-verification rounds draw fresh noise; the vocabulary-parallel
draft kernel kept the bare seed. Its drafts after step 0 therefore differed from
the full-vocab path, which test_vocab_parallel_draft_matches_full_vocab checks.
DSpark samples its drafts over the full vocabulary and is unaffected.

diff --git a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/vocab_parallel.py b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/vocab_parallel.py
index db0fbc14c..5ad268d52 100644
--- a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/vocab_parallel.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/vocab_parallel.py
